==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Those Guys]] spawn after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>, delay 6.67~13.33 seconds<sup>200f~400f</sup>.
*2 [[Gabriel]]s spawn after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>, delay 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>.
*1 [[Jackie Peng]] spawns after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Teacher Bun Bun]] spawns as the boss.
**15 [[Gabriel]]s spawn, delay 13.33~20 seconds<sup>400f~600f</sup>.
**6 [[Jackie Peng]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 40~46.67 seconds<sup>1,200f~1,400f</sup>.
**1 [[Ange Lackey]] spawns after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>.
**1 [[Master A.]] spawns after 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>.

==Strategy==
This stage introduces Ange Lackey, who is a decently difficult [[:Category:Sage Enemies|Sage]] enemy. Despite dealing relatively low damage, Lackey's guaranteed [[Explosion]] and Knockback can make them incredibly annoying to deal with. Not helping is their 750,000 HP and their 600 range which facilitates the use of rushers. However, [[Master of Logic Newtone (Special Cat)|Newtone]] is pretty good at chipping at them, while [[Idi:N (Special Cat)|Idi:NX]] and [[Talents|Talented]] [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] are suitable counters for them.

Despite this, this stage in particular isn't too difficult. After you build up your wallet and hit the base, lure the Bun Bun to your base and burst him as much as you can to avoid fighting him and Ange Lackey at the same time. Use Bahamut to chain Bun Bun while assisting him with meatshields like Boulder Cat and Manic Eraser Cat to stall him. Bahamut should be able to fully cycle Bun Bun with the assistance of a small Attack [[Cat Combo]], though if he fails to fully kill the Bun Bun you can supplement the remaining damage with [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jelly Dumpling Cat]], [[Bubble Cat]] and [[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fishman Cat]]. After that's done, beat up Ange Lackey with your rushers or [[Master of Mind Soractes (Special Cat)|Soractes]], then deal with the Master A. with a specific unit in your lineup like Newtone or [[Dogumaru (Special Cat)|Reborn Warrior Doguemon]].

==Trivia==
*Crunchy Cookie Canyon's Japanese name, Zakuzakukkī Sanmyaku (ザクザクッキー山脈, "Zakuzakookie Mountains"), contains a pun on ザクザク ''zakuzaku'' (a "crunchy" onomatopoeia that can refer to cutting into large pieces) and クッキー ''kukkī'' (cookie).

